        },
        {
            "block_label": "paragraph_title",
            "block_content": "Problem:Determine free-field blast wave parameters at a distance from a partially vented explosion inside a four wall cubicle.",
            "block_bbox": [
                134,
                382,
                980,
                434
            ],
            "block_id": 2,
            "block_order": 2
        },
        {
            "block_label": "paragraph_title",
            "block_content": "Procedure:",
            "block_bbox": [
                135,
                455,
                263,
                476
            ],
            "block_id": 3,
            "block_order": 3
        },
        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "Step 1.Determine charge weight, distance to point in question, vent area and volume of structure.\n",
            "block_bbox": [
                134,
                499,
                997,
                548
            ],
            "block_id": 4,
            "block_order": 4
        },
        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "Step 2.Apply a 20% safety factor to the charge weight.",
            "block_bbox": [
                134,
                569,
                768,
                595
            ],
            "block_id": 5,
            "block_order": 5
        },
        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "Step 3.Calculate distance Z,$A/V^{2/3}$ ratio and $A W^{1/3}/V\\mathrm{r a t i o}$ ",
            "block_bbox": [
                135,
                611,
                808,
                638
            ],
            "block_id": 6,
            "block_order": 6
        },
        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "Step 4.Determine peak positive pressure using Figure 2-184$(\\pm/\\underline{{\\pm}})$ ",
            "block_bbox": [
                135,
                659,
                891,
                684
            ],
            "block_id": 7,
            "block_order": 7
        },
        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "Step 5.Determine scaled positive impulses using Figure 2-185 (+). Multiply by $W^{1/3}$ to calculate actual value of impulses.\n",
            "block_bbox": [
                134,
                702,
                1005,
                753
            ],
            "block_id": 8,
            "block_order": 8
        },
        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "Step 6.Determine shock parameters from Figure 2-15 (+). Use the peak pressure from Step 4, except for normal reflected impulse where the scaled impulse(s) from Step 5 should be used.\n",
            "block_bbox": [
                134,
                773,
                1041,
                852
            ],
